            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="administrator-dashboard-access-transparency-disc">Administrator Dashboard Access &mdash; Transparency Disclosure</h2>
                <p>In the interest of complete honesty and transparency, we want you to know exactly who has elevated access to the CertiFried Dashboard and what that access entails.</p>
                <h3>Authorized Administrators</h3>
                <p>The following individuals have super-administrator access to the CertiFried MultiTool dashboard, which allows them to view guild settings, bot configurations, and server setup details for <strong>any server</strong> that has the bot installed:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>xXDeath420Xx</strong> (Discord ID: 365905620060340224) &mdash; Lead Developer &amp; Bot Owner</li>
                    <li><strong>Orsokuma (Bear)</strong> (Discord ID: 685127470625980501) &mdash; Co-Administrator &amp; Support Lead</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>What This Access Includes</h3>
                <p>Super-administrator dashboard access permits viewing of:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Guild configuration settings (channels, roles, feature toggles)</li>
                    <li>Bot setup and custom bot configurations</li>
                    <li>Streaming subscription and notification settings</li>
                    <li>Moderation, security, and logging configurations</li>
                    <li>Economy, leveling, and game system settings</li>
                    <li>Birthday card and community feature configurations</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>What This Access Does NOT Include</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Reading private messages or DM content</li>
                    <li>Accessing channels the bot does not have permission to see</li>
                    <li>Viewing Discord authentication tokens or OAuth credentials of any user</li>
                    <li>Modifying or managing your server without your knowledge</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Our Commitment</h3>
                <p>This access exists <strong>solely for the purpose of providing bot support</strong> &mdash; diagnosing issues, verifying configurations, and assisting server administrators with setup. We will <strong>never</strong> log in to, manage, or make changes to any user's guild without their <strong>express consent and knowledge</strong>. If support requires us to view or modify your settings, we will always ask for your permission first.</p>
                <p>By inviting CertiFried MultiTool to your Discord server, you acknowledge and agree to this access. If you have concerns or wish to discuss this policy, contact us through our Discord support server or at <a href="mailto:support@certifriedmultitool.com">support@certifriedmultitool.com</a>.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="group-greeting-cards-service">Group Greeting Cards Service</h2>
                <p>CertiFried offers a free standalone group greeting card service at <a href="/cards">certifriedmultitool.com/cards</a> that operates independently of Discord servers. By using the cards service, you agree to the following additional terms:</p>
                <h3>Card Creation &amp; Signing</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Cards can be created by anyone without an account. Cards created without a Discord login are "standalone" and can optionally be connected to a Discord server later.</li>
                    <li>Signing a card (adding a message, image, GIF, voice recording, or gift code) is available to both authenticated users and guests. Guests must provide a name.</li>
                    <li>All content submitted to cards (text, images, audio, GIFs) must comply with the Prohibited Activities section below. Explicit, NSFW, or illegal content is strictly prohibited.</li>
                    <li>Card creators and server administrators may delete individual signatures or entire cards at any time.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>AI-Generated Cover Images</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>AI cover images are generated with Google Gemini, or Hugging Face when Gemini cannot make one, and are subject to that provider's usage policies.</li>
                    <li>Generated images are stored on our servers and associated with the card. We do not claim ownership of AI-generated images.</li>
                    <li>Prompts are filtered to prevent generation of inappropriate content. Attempting to bypass content filters is a violation of these terms.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Encrypted Gift Card Codes</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Gift card codes attached to signatures are encrypted using AES-256-GCM before storage. The encrypted data is only decryptable by the card recipient or card creator via an authenticated request.</li>
                    <li>Gift codes are <strong>never displayed in page HTML</strong>, never logged, and never accessible to administrators. We cannot recover lost gift codes if the encryption key is compromised.</li>
                    <li>CertiFried is not responsible for the validity, value, or redemption of gift codes submitted by card signers. We do not sell, issue, or verify gift cards.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Voice Messages</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Voice recordings are captured via the browser's MediaRecorder API and uploaded as WebM audio files (max 30 seconds, max 2MB).</li>
                    <li>Voice recordings are stored on our servers alongside the card. They are deleted when the card or signature is deleted.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Discord Integration</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Standalone cards can be connected to a Discord server at any time by the card creator, preserving all existing signatures and content.</li>
                    <li>Connecting a card to Discord requires "Manage Server" permission on the target server and that the CertiFried bot is installed in that server.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="legal-section">
                <h2 id="greenhouse-tycoon">Greenhouse Tycoon</h2>
                <p>Greenhouse Tycoon is a plant-growing simulation game. It replaced CertiFried Tycoon; progress from that game was not carried over.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>No real value.</strong> In-game cash, plants, decorations, badges and rewards have no real-world value and cannot be bought, sold or exchanged for money or anything outside the game.</li>
                    <li><strong>No purchases.</strong> The game charges nobody; it does not use Bits, subscriptions or payments.</li>
                    <li><strong>One save.</strong> Twitch, Kick and Discord sign-ins can be linked to one save. Saves are never merged, and a Replant resets progress by your choice.</li>
                    <li><strong>Fair play.</strong> Do not use bots, scripts, multiple accounts or bugs to gain an advantage. We may correct balances, remove items, reset progress or exclude players who do.</li>
                    <li><strong>Seasons.</strong> Seasons, quests, challenges, prices and rewards may change, end early or be rebalanced. Season rewards are paid in game currency and badges only.</li>
                    <li><strong>Twitch panel.</strong> Use of the panel on Twitch is also subject to Twitch&rsquo;s Terms of Service. Sharing your Twitch ID with the panel is optional and can be revoked in Twitch&rsquo;s settings.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

