                <h2 id="stream-bot-studio-and-song-requests">Stream Bot, CertiFried Studio and Song Requests</h2>
                <p>The stream bot acts on your own Twitch, Kick and YouTube channels with the permissions you give it, and CertiFried Studio acts on your PC and in your OBS. By using them you also agree to the following:</p>
                <h3>Your channel, your responsibility</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>You are responsible for what your automations, timers and commands do and post, as if you had done it yourself. Test an automation (Dry run) before relying on it.</li>
                    <li>You must follow the terms and rules of every platform you connect, including Twitch&rsquo;s Terms of Service and Community Guidelines and Kick&rsquo;s Terms of Service and Community Guidelines. The YouTube features use YouTube API Services: by linking a YouTube channel you agree to be bound by the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a> applies to what Google does with your data. CertiFried cannot give you permission to do something a platform forbids.</li>
                    <li>Money is tracked, never processed. Tips, Bits, subs and orders are notifications of payments made on Twitch, Kick or the tip service; CertiFried does not handle, hold or refund money and never sees payment details. Questions about a payment go to the service it was made on.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Music, sounds and copyright</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>You are responsible for having the rights to the music, sounds, images and videos you play or show on stream, including song requests from your viewers, sound alerts and uploaded media. Copyright claims, takedowns, strikes and platform penalties are between you, the rights holder and the platform.</li>
                    <li>VOD protection is best effort. CertiFried Studio keeps song requests off your Twitch VOD track, but Twitch clips, Kick VODs, other platforms you stream to, local recordings and anything else on your VOD track can still contain the music. We do not promise that any song will avoid a claim.</li>
                    <li>If you choose to play song requests with your own Spotify account, note that Spotify&rsquo;s terms do not allow broadcasting its audio. That choice and its consequences are yours.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>CertiFried Studio</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Studio is published unsigned, with SHA-256 checksums on the <a href="/downloads/studio">download page</a>. Download it only from certifriedmultitool.com and check the checksum if you are unsure. The <a href="/eula#certifried-studio">EULA</a> covers the builds in more detail.</li>
                    <li>Studio changes your OBS only as described on <a href="/studio/how-it-works#changes-to-obs">How it works</a>, and backs up OBS files before it edits them. You remain responsible for your PC, your OBS setup and your stream.</li>
